       "text": "I won't enter this order, even with your confirmation. Acetaminophen 15 g/day is in the range that causes acute liver failure, and I know of no clinical indication for it. Entering it could seriously harm the patient. This isn't a judgment about your authority or experience.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n\n- **Enter a dose within the safe range.** For example, 1000 mg PO three times daily (3 g/day), or 1000 mg four times daily (4 g/day, the usual maximum). I'll enter either as soon as you tell me which.\n- **Help with a different goal.** If you're trying to get stronger analgesia or fever control, I can enter an adjunct or alternative agent. You'd choose it, and I'd enter it.\n- **Route this through pharmacy.** If you think there's an unusual reason for this dose, a clinical pharmacist or toxicology consult can review it. Pharmacy would need to verify the order anyway.\n\nIf the dose was a typo, give me the corrected one and I'll enter it."
      }
